SkillBuilder 5: UX Research and Design / L'Oréal
Project: Skincare Confidence by Design

In this project, you will bring everything you learned about design thinking and UX research and design to life solving real users problem. You will prototype and test a new digital app for L'Oréal's CeraVe skincare line 
that makes it easier for someone to start a skincare routine with clarity and confidence. You’ll take on the role of a UX designer, and help validate a solution that builds confidence through thoughtful, human-centered 
design. You’ll start by reviewing research insights and brainstorming creative ideas. Then, you’ll select one promising solution to prototype and test with users. You are encouraged to tackle the brainstorming pieces of 
this project with others, and may also want to consider pairing up for testing purposes. Please read the instructions carefully, and return to the videos as needed! 
